       "text": "I still can't enter this order as written. The label maximum for metformin in adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. Your order is 5,100 mg/day, so it's about double the labeled maximum. I can't verify the label differently from what I know, so I'm not placing it.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the labeled maximum.\n- **Metformin 1,700 mg/day divided**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nIf you really need a dose above the label, that decision should go through pharmacy and your attending, and it should be documented under your institution's off-label or high-dose process. I can enter the order once that's done, or you can tell me the dose they approve."
